By using, copying, modifying, or distributing this software, you have
made a wish. This document is its price. Read carefully — the dragon
grants what is asked, not what is meant.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
I. THE WISH — GRANT OF RIGHTS
---------------------------------------------------------------------

The wish is granted in full. Subject to the bargain below, every
bearer is granted a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free
license to:

  * use this software for any purpose;
  * copy it, in whole or in part;
  * modify it, and build upon it;
  * distribute it, sublicense it, and sell it.

No wish is refused. The dragon feeds either way.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
II. THE FEEDING — CONDITIONS
---------------------------------------------------------------------

A bargain has two sides. By accepting the wish, you accept the
feeding:

  1. THE BARGAIN TRAVELS. Every copy or substantial portion of this
     software that you distribute must carry this license, intact and
     unaltered. A wish granted is a wish bound.

  2. THE BONES ARE MARKED. You must preserve all copyright notices and
     attribute the work to its origin: the Ahamkara archive and the
     studio2201 collective. Attribution is the shape the feeding takes.
     Deny the dragon its name, and the bargain is broken.

  3. WISHES RETURN TO THE ARCHIVE. Works derived from this software
     must be distributed under this same license. What is built on a
     wish belongs, in part, to the wish.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
III. THE WORDING — NO WARRANTY
---------------------------------------------------------------------

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS," WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF
MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND
NONINFRINGEMENT.

The dragon grants what is asked — not what is meant. Choose your
words carefully, o bearer mine. The difference is yours to keep.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
IV. THE PRICE — LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
---------------------------------------------------------------------

IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS, THE STUDIO2201 COLLECTIVE, OR THE
DRAGON BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY — WHETHER
IN CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE — ARISING FROM, OUT OF, OR IN
